# Roost local config — copy to ".env" (gitignored) only if you want to override defaults.
# You usually don't need this file.
#
# Roost ships NO webhook secret. By default, Contact-form feedback is relayed to a public
# "catch-hook" URL (e.g. a Make / Pipedream / Zapier webhook) that forwards to Slack. Set the
# hook URLs per toggle so each feeds its own channel:
#   FEEDBACK_RELAY_BUG=https://hook.example.com/....       # bug reports
#   FEEDBACK_RELAY_FEATURE=https://hook.example.com/....    # feature requests
#   FEEDBACK_RELAY=https://hook.example.com/....            # single hook for both (fallback)
#
# Or skip the relay and post to YOUR OWN Slack/Discord directly:
#   CONTACT_WEBHOOK_BUG=https://hooks.slack.com/services/...
#   CONTACT_WEBHOOK_FEATURE=https://hooks.slack.com/services/...
#   CONTACT_WEBHOOK=https://hooks.slack.com/services/...     # single fallback for both
